{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.68,"content_digest":"0eda09f0da67a9655285617667f7872188932941007a37eee46d2632df337d74","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:02:36+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"d2a67e6a96c2154bdc4dbab24f668ecfc9b30ccff48c73d584e98cae38a97007","input_tokens":6195,"latency_ms":37102,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"790494d68ec0aee25267680276339fdfbca7439fe620697058ea34cb01074fc7","output_tokens":2444,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:07024bd5f51ae62978e929b8","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:causation-intervention","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QBDC0ZQ3CFD8DRQ9EY8C8T","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle shows that statistical indistinguishability under evaluation is an associational fact that does not imply invariance under the deployment intervention; this aligns with the meta-principle that causal claims require interventional reasoning rather than association alone.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:02:36+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.62,"content_digest":"c2e105a3cca3df412a768ad2ba0a0a8015ee76d6d53b893006960c615ef6c088","created_at":"2026-08-23T05:21:42+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"bcf8d15514dcb063f959bb76932dfbe4284fbc0ba4b3f244311ffc62776a697e","input_tokens":5641,"latency_ms":29724,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"22716521f30f2e47916d531fcd173bccfe6bea423d9e309270080de98072b6eb","output_tokens":2332,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:2524827b31d7c4df5133945a","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:data-quality-ceiling","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:scientific-discovery:01M0PH1N050A14188R7MNYY9JC","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The Go move-prediction claim is a concrete case of the data-quality ceiling: a local dynamical system lacking an explicit life concept cannot recover the two-eye life distinction, so the missing concept must be supplied explicitly. The meta-principle's coverage-gap logic directly applies to this representational absence, and the study-bound scope is compatible with the meta-principle's task-dependent boundary.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T05:21:42+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.82,"content_digest":"4fe7937ce014b7077b7b959c2ba822d7c50dfd56da8c6dc85a18ecf3952464e9","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:44:03+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:6743c6a3bef8dbf21ec71ffb","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:distribution-shift","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:general:01M0AWAF7S75SY89A5T4QS49G2","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The distribution-shift meta-principle establishes that performance under a test distribution different from the training distribution is not guaranteed and requires assumptions; the observed lower performance of LLM evaluators on OOD data is a specific manifestation of this general boundary. The meta-principle bounds the expectation of OOD evaluation capability without asserting the exact drop, leaving the empirical magnitude to the study.","relation_type":"bounded_by","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:44:03+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"partial","confidence":0.5,"content_digest":"622ea2c82c319472482eb5d62ad4a4f41e0e595961e5ebaee3f77b84441144ca","created_at":"2026-08-23T07:16:50+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"006f5f1e334fa7c756243dbb8809cbb01cb80508c72e5c9005dc3f125ef24da4","input_tokens":5632,"latency_ms":47006,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"a7b687b43fe16dfc1702e1e68ff9697d5cfd61d9c24ee88b9b06793abaab1529","output_tokens":2599,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:bd4aaa25110467bb10c9fe85","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:parsimony-mdl","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0PQKY9V3CKV8A8P2M1VTFCN","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"MDL balances model complexity against data-fit cost. A higher-order n-gram model carries a larger model cost and may not reduce data cost enough on small corpora, so the lower-order model can have better predictive compression, consistent with the observed perplexity outcome.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T07:16:50+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.82,"content_digest":"e14ddc108310c54b5174330cd53e90a00a8432f650d10f5ea8b77c6e10c53392","created_at":"2026-08-23T05:22:09+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"5337c122d0a7ea1f7cc2221d0e8081fd9fc72f143758e1edb1d53ea6e5778684","input_tokens":5878,"latency_ms":26842,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"1cf00200d8e375f2ecf2f992918148d17dab03f40f5b3d2d05b52be6d38ea24a","output_tokens":2552,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:c0b76e1b73b4009b9cef9ed2","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:test-time-compute","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:scientific-discovery:01M0PH2JC32YVANQ86WWWTWD5G","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle is a specific application of test-time compute allocation: it identifies game phases and position types where investing computation in a local dynamical-system engine yields better accuracy or cost tradeoffs relative to MCTS. This matches the meta-principle's claim that gains from inference-time compute depend on problem difficulty, model quality, verifier, latency, and budget.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T05:22:09+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.85,"content_digest":"81debb44b19ff70e43fd418ef9557d72934805da08777e242ef188614390cf5e","created_at":"2026-08-22T19:30:10+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"827896f84a25c532c2d1d5177cfb1b4695bd9bcc09fac8b9f95c0991bb104d53","input_tokens":5611,"latency_ms":17181,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"9af9f6fb3712422ecac69e993a8bdae6fb5d1df1f06b5dac26e3c0cb217f34b9","output_tokens":2739,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:d63f5484de7ee8cfa709ba66","meta_principle_id":"meta:neuroscience-cognition:sparse-coding","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:neuroscience-cognition:01M0NF6XATFSPGC4151CJAYZW7","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle is a specific empirical finding within sparse coding: it concerns sparse coding models learning V1-like edge filters and states that algorithm identity is secondary when sparse representations are sufficiently efficient and data-adapted. This refines the general sparse-coding principle that learning sparse generative models of natural images produces localized receptive fields resembling visual cortex.","relation_type":"specializes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T02:58:57+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0P5WC937PV7PKQMASBZ4D3Z"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T19:30:10+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
